From: Darrel Griët <dgriet@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] v10: Report minnow's real 45Hz vsync period

minnow's HWC_VSYNC_PERIOD query always fails, so refreshRate() fell
back to assuming 60 Hz. The panel really runs at 45 Hz (pixel clock
4176 kHz / 320x290), so Qt's fixed-step animation driver advanced
animations by 16.7 ms per frame while real frames arrive every
22.2 ms. Flick/fling animations therefore played at ~75% speed and
visibly hitched whenever the driver drift-corrected back to wall
time. The wrong rate was also advertised to Wayland clients through
wl_output, giving every app the same wrong animation timestep.

Report the true 22.2 ms period instead. Minnow-only: the correct
fallback is specific to this panel.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [minnow-specific panel timing]
---
--- a/hwcomposer/hwcomposer_backend_v10.cpp	2026-07-18 16:00:00.000000000 +0200
+++ b/hwcomposer/hwcomposer_backend_v10.cpp	2026-07-18 16:00:00.000000000 +0200
@@ -354,8 +354,8 @@

         int res = hwc_device->query(hwc_device, HWC_VSYNC_PERIOD, &vsyncVal);
         if (res != 0 || vsyncVal == 0) {
-            qWarning() << "query(HWC_VSYNC_PERIOD) failed, assuming 60 Hz";
-            vsyncVal = 16666667; // 60 Hz vsync period in ns
+            qWarning() << "query(HWC_VSYNC_PERIOD) failed, assuming 45 Hz";
+            vsyncVal = 22222222; // minnow panel: 4176 kHz / (320*290) = 45 Hz
         }

         vsyncFPS = (float)1000000000 / (float)vsyncVal;
